{{!-- Token Stealth Configuration — GM only.

      Organised by the QUESTION each group answers rather than by which
      variable it sets, because the two dials people actually reach for
      (how far, how long) are independent by design and everything else is
      a refinement of one of them.

      Every field here is read by the live model. The legacy passive-vs-roll
      model's controls — range bands, vision zones, coverage mods, base sight —
      were removed with that model. --}}
<div class="wdm-stealth-config-body wdm-stress-config-body">

  <header class="wdm-se-head">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-user-ninja"></i> {{localize 'WITCHER.App.StealthConfig.Title'}}</h2>
    <p class="wdm-se-blurb">Each watcher projects a <b>cone</b> whose size is fixed
      by your Stealth against their Awareness, plus the light and weather. Inside
      that cone you roll Stealth once per tick — guards never roll. Missing the
      roll fills their eye; a full eye means they've found you.</p>
  </header>

  {{!-- ================= CORE ================= --}}
  <details class="wdm-se-group" open>
    <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-toggle-on"></i> {{localize 'WITCHER.App.StealthConfig.Section.Core'}}</summary>
    <div class="wdm-sc-checks">
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="enabled" data-config-key="enabled" {{#if values.enabled}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>Enable stealth</b><br>
          <small class="wdm-sc-help">Off = no checks, no cones, no HUD. Existing stealth states are kept.</small></span>
      </label>
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="crossLevelDetection" data-config-key="crossLevelDetection" {{#if values.crossLevelDetection}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>See between floors</b><br>
          <small class="wdm-sc-help">Whether watchers on another level can spot you.</small></span>
      </label>
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="debug" data-config-key="debug" {{#if values.debug}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>Debug output</b><br>
          <small class="wdm-sc-help">Verbose GM logging. <code>wdmStealthWhy()</code> in the console prints the full breakdown per watcher.</small></span>
      </label>
    </div>
  </details>

  {{!-- ================= HOW FAR ================= --}}
  <details class="wdm-se-group" open>
    <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-eye-low-vision"></i> How far people get noticed</summary>
    <p class="wdm-se-blurb">These set the <b>size of the cone</b>. None of them
      change how long you survive once inside it.</p>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Notice distance (m)</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" min="1" name="dBaseMetres" data-config-key="dBaseMetres" value="{{values.dBaseMetres}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">The reach of an average watcher
        against an average sneak, in daylight, looking straight at them. Everything
        below scales this. Raise if people cross open ground unnoticed; lower if
        cones swamp the map.</small>
    </div>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Darkness strength</span>
        <input type="number" step="0.05" min="0.01" max="0.5" name="lightStep" data-config-key="lightStep" value="{{values.lightStep}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">Reach removed per step of
        darkness. 0.2 → dim −1 keeps 80%, dim −2 60%, dim −3 40%, darkness 20%,
        pitch black nothing. Night Vision waives the dim tiers outright; Improved
        also waives darkness; Dark Vision sees in pitch out to its own range.</small>
    </div>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Skill weight</span>
        <input type="number" step="0.01" min="1.01" name="skillBase" data-config-key="skillBase" value="{{values.skillBase}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">Cone size per point of
        (their Awareness − your Stealth). 1.12 means every 5 points roughly halves
        it. Deliberately capped between ½× and 2× — your Stealth is <i>also</i> in
        the roll, and letting it swing the cone as well made high Stealth
        untouchable.</small>
    </div>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Night sight cap (m)</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" min="1" name="nightCeilingMetres" data-config-key="nightCeilingMetres" value="{{values.nightCeilingMetres}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">Nobody notices anyone beyond
        this at night, however brightly lit they are. Darkvision overrides it —
        it's a purchased ability to see further.</small>
    </div>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Vision arc (°)</span>
        <input type="number" step="5" min="1" max="360" name="defaultVisionAngleDeg" data-config-key="defaultVisionAngleDeg" value="{{values.defaultVisionAngleDeg}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">Cone width for tokens with no
        vision angle set.</small>
    </div>

    <div class="wdm-sc-checks">
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="clipOverlayToOwnFov" data-config-key="clipOverlayToOwnFov" {{#if values.clipOverlayToOwnFov}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>Hide cones in your own blind spot</b><br>
          <small class="wdm-sc-help">On: the overlay is clipped to what your
            selected character can actually see, so nothing is drawn behind
            them. Off: cones show all around you.</small></span>
      </label>
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="fullCircleIsUnset" data-config-key="fullCircleIsUnset" {{#if values.fullCircleIsUnset}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>Treat 360° as "not configured"</b><br>
          <small class="wdm-sc-help">On: a token left at Foundry's default 360°
            uses the arc above, instead of projecting a full circle. Off: 360°
            is taken literally. The per-token True Angle flag always wins.</small></span>
      </label>
    </div>
  </details>

  {{!-- ================= HOW LONG ================= --}}
  <details class="wdm-se-group" open>
    <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-hourglass-half"></i> How long you last inside one</summary>
    <p class="wdm-se-blurb">These decide what happens <b>inside</b> the cone. None
      of them change its size.</p>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Exposure to spot</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" min="1" name="threshold" data-config-key="threshold" value="{{values.threshold}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">A failed roll adds however much
        it missed by. At this total the watcher has you. Raise if people are caught
        too fast; lower if guards feel oblivious.</small>
    </div>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Forget rate</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" min="0" name="exposureDecayPerTick" data-config-key="exposureDecayPerTick" value="{{values.exposureDecayPerTick}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">Suspicion drained per tick once
        you're out of their cone.</small>
    </div>

    <p class="wdm-se-blurb" style="margin-top:.5rem"><b>Depth penalties.</b> How
      much your roll suffers by how deep into the cone you stand. Steep on purpose
      — without it, a high Stealth score is untouchable at arm's length.</p>
    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Outer</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="tierModifiers.outer" data-config-key="tierModifiers.outer" value="{{values.tierModifiers.outer}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Mid</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="tierModifiers.mid" data-config-key="tierModifiers.mid" value="{{values.tierModifiers.mid}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Inner</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="tierModifiers.inner" data-config-key="tierModifiers.inner" value="{{values.tierModifiers.inner}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Core</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="tierModifiers.core" data-config-key="tierModifiers.core" value="{{values.tierModifiers.core}}" /></label>
    </div>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Point blank (m)</span>
        <input type="number" step="0.5" min="0" name="pointBlankMetres" data-config-key="pointBlankMetres" value="{{values.pointBlankMetres}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">Inside this you're seen with no
        roll at all — proximity is a fact, not a contest. Pitch darkness is the one
        exception.</small>
    </div>
    <div class="wdm-sc-checks">
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="pointBlankAutoSpot" data-config-key="pointBlankAutoSpot" {{#if values.pointBlankAutoSpot}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>Point blank is automatic</b><br>
          <small class="wdm-sc-help">Off = a brutal penalty instead of a certainty,
            so an extraordinary sneak can try it.</small></span>
      </label>
    </div>
  </details>

  {{!-- ================= WHAT HELPS YOU ================= --}}
  <details class="wdm-se-group">
    <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i> What helps you hide</summary>
    <p class="wdm-se-blurb">Bonuses added to your roll. Higher = better hidden.</p>

    <p class="wdm-se-blurb"><b>Cover</b> — by how much of you is visible.</p>
    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>In the open</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="coverBonuses.exposed" data-config-key="coverBonuses.exposed" value="{{values.coverBonuses.exposed}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>¾ visible</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="coverBonuses.threeQuarter" data-config-key="coverBonuses.threeQuarter" value="{{values.coverBonuses.threeQuarter}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Half</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="coverBonuses.half" data-config-key="coverBonuses.half" value="{{values.coverBonuses.half}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Quarter</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="coverBonuses.quarter" data-config-key="coverBonuses.quarter" value="{{values.coverBonuses.quarter}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>A sliver</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="coverBonuses.sliver" data-config-key="coverBonuses.sliver" value="{{values.coverBonuses.sliver}}" /></label>
    </div>

    <p class="wdm-se-blurb"><b>Movement</b> — measured from ground covered per tick,
      never declared.</p>
    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Still</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="paceBonuses.still" data-config-key="paceBonuses.still" value="{{values.paceBonuses.still}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Creeping</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="paceBonuses.creep" data-config-key="paceBonuses.creep" value="{{values.paceBonuses.creep}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Walking</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="paceBonuses.walk" data-config-key="paceBonuses.walk" value="{{values.paceBonuses.walk}}" /></label>
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled"><span>Running</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="paceBonuses.run" data-config-key="paceBonuses.run" value="{{values.paceBonuses.run}}" /></label>
    </div>

    <div class="wdm-sc-inline">
      <label class="wdm-se-mini wdm-sc-mini-labeled">
        <span>Prone</span>
        <input type="number" step="1" name="postureProne" data-config-key="postureBonuses.prone" value="{{values.postureProne}}" />
      </label>
      <small class="wdm-sc-help wdm-sc-help-inline">Applied while the token has the
        Prone status. Darkness is handled by the light ladder above, not here.</small>
    </div>
  </details>

  {{!-- ================= FEEDBACK ================= --}}
  <details class="wdm-se-group">
    <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-comment"></i> Feedback</summary>
    <div class="wdm-sc-checks">
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="rollChatCard" data-config-key="rollChatCard" {{#if values.rollChatCard}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>Post each tick's rolls</b><br>
          <small class="wdm-sc-help">One card per tick showing the roll, the DC and
            every modifier. Watchers are not named — the DC says "this one is
            sharp" without pointing him out on the map.</small></span>
      </label>
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="spottedChatCard" data-config-key="spottedChatCard" {{#if values.spottedChatCard}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>Announce being spotted</b></span>
      </label>
      <label class="wdm-se-check">
        <input type="checkbox" name="hideConeWhenSpotted" data-config-key="hideConeWhenSpotted" {{#if values.hideConeWhenSpotted}}checked{{/if}} />
        <span><b>Hide the cone once spotted</b><br>
          <small class="wdm-sc-help">Their eye stays red either way.</small></span>
      </label>
    </div>
  </details>

</div>
